# ShiftReport desktop - optional configuration guide
# Copy this file to .env beside desktop_gui.py (beside the executable when bundled).
# To use a separate file: python desktop_gui.py --env .env.raw
# Windows Python 3.8 launcher: py -3.8 desktop_gui.py --env .env.raw
#
# Syntax:
# - Lines beginning with # are comments. Remove # to enable an optional setting.
# - Use one KEY=VALUE per line, with each active key appearing only once.
# - Single/double quotes around a value are optional; UTF-8 Arabic text is accepted.
# - Put comments on their own lines, never after a value.
# - Values are literal: no ${VARIABLE}, %VARIABLE%, ~ or shell expansion.
# - Relative paths start beside the script/executable, even with --env elsewhere.
# - Examples below are placeholders; replace them with your own project values.
#
# This file is optional. Without it, the app uses defaults and a join-file picker.
# .env and .env.* are ignored by Git. Keep filled credentials out of your bundle.

# CONNECTION METHOD
# join (default): use the protected Android-exported .srjoin.json file.
# raw: occasional admin use with the credentials in the commented section below.
# Change the existing line to raw; do not add a second CONNECTION_MODE line.
CONNECTION_MODE=join

# JOIN-FILE MODE
# Blank opens a file picker. Otherwise use an existing protected join file.
# The app always prompts for its password; do not put the password here.
# For raw mode this MUST be blank.
JOIN_FILE=
# JOIN_FILE=project.srjoin.json
# JOIN_FILE="C:/ShiftReport/project.srjoin.json"
# JOIN_FILE="/home/yourname/ShiftReport/project.srjoin.json"

# TIME AND LOCAL STORAGE (both connection methods)
# IANA time zone used for dates and the 08:30 shift boundary. Match your hospital.
# Examples: Asia/Damascus, Asia/Riyadh, UTC.
TIMEZONE=Asia/Damascus

# Blank chooses the platform's normal app-data directory:
# Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%/ShiftReportDesktop
# Linux: $XDG_DATA_HOME/ShiftReportDesktop, or ~/.local/share/ShiftReportDesktop
# These descriptions use OS variable notation; DATA_DIR itself does not expand it.
# Contains encrypted SQLite drafts, receipts and local key protection files.
# Keep this directory stable; choosing another one does not move existing data.
DATA_DIR=
# DATA_DIR="C:/ShiftReport/workspace"
# DATA_DIR="/home/yourname/.local/share/ShiftReportDesktop"

# PDF FONT
# Blank searches Windows Arial or common Linux DejaVu/Noto TrueType fonts.
# Override with an existing Arabic-capable .ttf file, using a full or relative path.
PDF_FONT=
# PDF_FONT="C:/Windows/Fonts/arial.ttf"
# PDF_FONT="/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf"
# PDF_FONT="fonts/ArabicFont.ttf"

# APPEARANCE AND ARABIC DISPLAY
# Appearance choices: System (default), Light, Dark.
APPEARANCE=System
# APPEARANCE=Light
# APPEARANCE=Dark

# auto (default): shape Arabic for Linux display; retain Windows native behavior.
# native: let Tk handle display; choose this if your Tk already handles Arabic.
# shaped: force the Arabic presentation adapter for labels and read-only text.
# These options do not change saved Unicode, Telegram payloads or PDF rendering.
# Editable text keeps native Tk editing; forms provide a shaped Arabic readback.
TEXT_RENDERING=auto
# TEXT_RENDERING=native
# TEXT_RENDERING=shaped

# OPTIONAL RAW CREDENTIALS (admin startup only)
# To enable: change CONNECTION_MODE above to raw, keep JOIN_FILE blank, then
# uncomment and fill each required field below. Leave these commented in join mode.
# A current doctor-registry admin must verify a private Telegram code BEFORE the
# local workspace opens. Shared actions recheck admin status and membership.
# Raw startup needs internet. It does not create a project or doctor registry:
# publish the registry from Android first. Normal join mode supports other members.
# Existing-session reconnect still uses a protected join file for the same project.
# You may copy this same guide to .env.raw and select it with --env .env.raw.
#
# Display name used in the desktop project status and report captions (required).
# HOSPITAL_NAME="Your hospital name"
#
# Current bot token from BotFather (required). No quotes within the actual token.
# BOT_TOKEN=
#
# Existing hospital Telegram group ID: a negative integer, often starting -100.
# CHAT_ID=
#
# Existing topic IDs: integer message-thread IDs, not Telegram URLs (required).
# REPORTS: general report destination; CSV: clinical synchronization documents;
# DOCTORS: doctor registry topic. Use the EXACT Android project values.
# Use 0 only where the existing project does not use a topic; never guess an ID.
# REPORTS_TOPIC_ID=
# CSV_TOPIC_ID=
# DOCTORS_TOPIC_ID=
#
# Optional announcements topic; omitted defaults to 0.
# ANNOUNCEMENTS_TOPIC_ID=0
#
# Explicitly match the existing project's encryption setting (required in raw mode).
# Unencrypted project: ENCRYPT_TELEGRAM=false and TELEGRAM_DATA_KEY blank.
# Encrypted project: ENCRYPT_TELEGRAM=true and its ORIGINAL Base64 32-byte key.
# This is not the join-file password, login code or local draft passphrase.
# Never generate a replacement key or turn encryption off to bypass a failure.
# ENCRYPT_TELEGRAM=
# TELEGRAM_DATA_KEY=
#
# Join passwords, Telegram login codes and Linux draft passphrases are entered
# interactively. There are no .env settings for them or for granting admin status.
# Raw mode stores plaintext secrets in this file; keep it private. Client admin
# checks cannot restrict someone using an extracted bot token directly in Telegram.
# To revoke a suspected token, use BotFather; editing this file does not revoke it.
